{
  "why": "Sea Shanty II, by ear. Key pins (audio time, lane 0-3 = D F J K): every intro (0:00, 0:09.6, 1:16.8, 1:26.4, 1:55.2, 2:04.8) in groups, each group's notes in pitch order, resetting between groups, no key twice in a row and no ghosts: K J F D | F D F J K J | K J F D | F D F J | K J F D | F D F J K J | K J F | J F J K | J F D | K J F (user, Nov 27, picking it over a ghost-key version: 'option 2 is better. let's do that'). The main theme (0:19.4, 0:57.8, 1:36.2, 2:14.6), from the user's taps: its first half on its four pitches in order, 69 D 71 F 73 J 74 K, the opening J F J J, and the four-note grace figures J {J K J} F, 73 {73 74 73} 71 ('It should be J{JKJ}F'); its second half 74 D 76 F 78 J 80 K, the repeated 76s all on F ('They should all be on the same key'). The eighth-note runs that open the second half (0:29, 0:33.8) F D F F F D F J K (user, Nov 27: 'it should be FD F F FD F J K'). The theme's closing C# B A on J F D, then the high A on K (user, Nov 27: 'the last note is a high note, so it should jump to K'). The strings bit's first two bars (0:38.6) FFFF JJJJ FFFF DFJFK J J F D (user, Nov 28: 'let's go with FFFF JJJJ FFFF DFJFK J J F D'). Bars 3-4 of the strings bit (0:45.9) JJJ JJJ F FFFF (user, Nov 28). The strings bit's second half (0:49.4) a copy of its first half's keys (user, Nov 28). Plus one extra J at 0:55.95 in its six J's (user, Nov 28). The quiet theme's accordion in place of its first melody strand (0:57.8), J FJ FJ FF JJ FF J FF JJ FF JJ FF JJ FF JJ (user, Nov 28). In every intro the run up 73 74 76 78 and its turn, F D F J K J, the four keys not enough for a five-note climb (user, Nov 28: 'at 1:23.5~, there's a DFJKFJ, and it's a run up with the last note being down... maybe FDFJKJ instead? see how that plays'). And the intro's first run up, 73 74 76 78 80 and its turn to 76, the same way, F D F J K J (user, Nov 28: 'There's two patterns, one does DFJFJD and one does FDFJK... The second is preferable, and it should be like that everywhere that pattern happens'). The ending K then a last low A on D at 2:33.84 (user, Nov 28: 'it should be K D').",
